* {{audio|De-Bauer.ogg|audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aʊ̯ɐ|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|de|bʰuH}}
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|būre}}, {{m|gmh|gebūre}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|būr}}, {{m|goh|gibūr}}, {{m|goh|gibūro}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*būraz}}. Compare English {{m|en|bower}}, {{m|en|boor}}, Dutch {{m|nl|boer}}, {{m|nl|buur}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Bauern|Bauern}}

# [[farmer]], [[peasant]], [[boor]]
# {{label|de|chess}} [[pawn]]

=====Usage notes=====
* ''Bauer'' is a weak noun in the standard language, but is part of a group of nouns which have a stark tendency to be strong colloquially, so one will often hear ''dem Bauer'' instead of ''dem Bauern''.

